solution:
The correct answer is **__-1__.**

**Given:**

Object distance u is -40cm and focal length is -20cm as it is converging.

**To find:**

Magnification of the image produced

**Formula:**

m=-{vover u}

{1over f}={1over v}+{1over u}

**Calculations:**

As, the mirror formula

{1over f}={1over v}+{1over u}

{1over -20}={1over v}+{1over -40}

{1over v}={1over -20}-{1over -40}

{1over v}={-2 + 1over 40}={1over -40}

v= - 40cm

Therefore, the magnification produced is

m=-{vover u}=-{-40over -40}=-1

Thus, the magnification produced is **-1.**
